00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,500
A · MARTHE V. — fictional witness · staged · seg A 00:14.0–00:18.0
The last train was the 18:40. A woman got off it holding a sealed envelope.

2
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:36,000
A · MARTHE V. — fictional witness · staged · seg A 00:18.0–00:22.5
The bell rang first. Then she opened the envelope and put the brass key on the bench.

3
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,500
A · MARTHE V. — fictional witness · staged · seg A 00:22.5–00:26.0
She walked away. The service door stayed shut; nobody came to open it.

4
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,000
A · MARTHE V. — fictional witness · staged · seg A 00:26.0–00:28.0
An old train. The last one that stopped there.

5
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,500
B · PAUL R. — fictional witness · staged · seg B 01:02.0–01:04.5
She stepped off the last train with a sealed envelope, and opened it on the bench.

6
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,000
B · PAUL R. — fictional witness · staged · seg B 01:04.5–01:07.0
She set the brass key down on the bench first.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,200
B · PAUL R. — fictional witness · staged · seg B 01:07.0–01:10.5
The bell only rang as the train pulled out.

8
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:49,500
B · PAUL R. — fictional witness · staged · seg B 01:10.5–01:13.0
The service door stayed shut. She went away.
